  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated production of rice and secondary crops using an agroecological approach in the Tandjil&#xc3;&#xa9; province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support transformation of food systems that improve food security and protect their natural resource base with focus on production of rice and secondary crops in Tandjil&#xc3;&#xa9; Province.
Targets:
&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#xa2;	Target 1.1: Improve livelihoods for 19,000 small-scale producers and rural dwellers, including 10,450 women and 8,550 men.
&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#xa2;	Target 1.2: Ensure 500 other beneficiaries directly benefit from the project, with at least 40% women, representing a minimum of 5 institutions, including at least 3 women-oriented organizations.
&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#xa2;	Target 2: Restore 2,000 hectares of land through sustainable land use practices.
&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#xa2;	Target 3: Improve land use practices on 10,000 hectares, excluding protected areas.
&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#xa2;	Target 4: Achieve or surpass 316,175 metric tons of carbon equivalent in emissions sequestered or avoided in agriculture, forestry, and other land use (AFOLU), confirmed by a second field assessment for scalability in the region.
&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#xa2;	Target 5: Strengthen 3 agricultural value chains (rice, sesame, groundnut) through innovative and inclusive business models.</narrative>
  </description>
